      "context_en": "Questions 446-453 are based on the following clinical case: At her perimenopausal age, Ms. Maher complains of anxiety, and intermittent, alternating feelings of heat and cold over the whole body. She has been taking various antianxiety medications, which seem to be of little help. Her heat and cold sensations can occur at the same time, but in different parts of the body. She often feels hot with a swelling sensation in the forehead, upper back, lateral sides of the arms, front thighs, and both knees. She also feels cold in the lower back, calves, and soles of the feet. These feelings of heat and cold come and go in an irregular way, and may become aggravated after strong emotional upset. Her appetite is poor, despite often feeling hungry. Her sleep is dream-disturbed, sometimes with nightmares. She has frequent urination and is constipated. Her urine is pale, and her stools are loose. Her tongue is red with slightly yellow, greasy coating, and her pulse is deep, thready and rapid.",
