      "question_en": "Last night, Mr. Pan, 59 years old, suddenly developed the following manifestations: watery diarrhea for five times, abdominal pain, borborygmus, an aversion to cold, fever, headache, pain in the extremities, nausea, vomiting, poor appetite, a sensation of fullness and oppression in the chest and abdomen, listlessness, fatigue. He has white greasy tongue coating, and a floating and wiry pulse. What would be the syndrome?",
